{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1504078-sidereal-death-perception-sight-sidereal-awareness-charms","id":1504078,"title":"Sidereal Death Perception Sight (Sidereal Awareness charms)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-28T15:30:18-08:00","id":1504078,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon6.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Sidereal Death Perception Sight (Sidereal Awareness charms)","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Sensing the Strings</span></b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 4m 1WP; <b>Mins</b>: Awareness 4, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type</b>: Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Divination<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms</b>: Prior Warning<br /> <br /> <i>The Sidereal closes their eyes and attunes their senses to that of the Loom of Fate, granting an strange yet new way of seeing the world.</i><br /> <br /> Upon activating this charm and closing their eyes, the Sidereal sees the world as the Loom of Fate sees it, a world of countless threads all connected to one another. Learning to sense using this method takes time, but it will only be a matter of time for a Sidereal to stop seeing individual strings and things like people, apples, trees, and other useful information. The Sidereal gains the following benefits:<ul><li>The Sidereal \u201csees\u201d things as strings. At a glance the Sidereal can gleam information such as what a target is, what they look like, what they are wearing, how far they are away, and any other relevant information. The Sidereal remains blind to information contained within such objects. A Sidereal\u2019s string sight might tell him the book he\u2019s holding is called the Thousand Correct Actions, but it will not tell him the content of the book. This specific use of the sense is accurate to as far as someone with Enhanced Sight could see, and can see as far as those with Magical sight can see when Opening the Ninth Eye is active.</li> <li>The Sidereal may \u201cfeel\u201d these strings out to a range of short 360 degrees around them. Allowing the Sidereal to see through any solid object as if it were transparent. Wards block this sight, but allow the Sidereal to see the wards.</li> <li>Enemies of Fate can still be sensed with this charm, but appear like a black siloette would for those with standard sight. Such a thing imposes no penalties in combat, but the Sidereal cannot make rolls to identify the target.</li> </ul>This counts as an exotic sense type that is considered Acute and Enhanced for charm purposes (See <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1G6YAQg493MBsHtRAwJ6kvughI3nVj5pc7yS4zHQX2lc/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Awareness revamp</a> for details on sense information).<br /> <br /> <b>Special Activation Conditions</b>: This charm is reduced to 1m 1WP if the character is blind. Alternatively, a Sidereal may train themselves to use this charm as if they were blind. The process takes one week during which time the Sidereal is counted as Blind (Sight) with all the usual penalties. Any significant amount of time using their eyes will remove the discount this charm provides. Superficial actions, such as opening their eyes in surprise or giving a playful wink do not count, as does opening their eyes for a moment to read a sentence or quick glance at a picture.<br /> <br /> <b>I wanted to give Sidereals the ability to join in on the blind swordsman trope, but bruh Perfection of the Visionary Warrior is Essence 5 and hella expensive.<br /> <br /> This kills several birds with one stone: It allows blind Sidereals, it grants a new &quot;Sidereal-y&quot; way to see the world like Matrix code, allows a charm for sharper senses, and allows Sidereals to work within the sense type paradigm I've made with my other homebrew.\u200b<br /> <br /> Also to clarify, one can &quot;see&quot; with this charm as normal distances, but it is only when someone comes within short range does the ability to see through walls activate.</b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Opening the Ninth Eye</span></b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 3m (6m 1WP); <b>Mins</b>: Awareness 5, Essence 3<br /> <b>Type</b>: Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: None<br /> <b>Duration</b>: One scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms</b>: Sensing the Strings<br /> <br /> <i>The Sidereal opens the illusive Ninth Eye of Enlightenment for Pattern Spiders, seeing the world in a way that only the Maidens can see.</i><br /> <br /> This charm may be activated whenever the Sidereal is using Sensing the Strings. The Sidereal opens their eyes, which are now a rainbow hue but still primarily their signature caste colour. Any eye coverings such as sunglasses and blindfolds also need to be removed; even blind characters need to open their eyes as the symbolic nature of this charm\u2019s themes is required to activate it. The Sidereal gains access to the following benefits:<ul><li>The unique sense type granted by Sensing the Strings is now Magical. Any attempt to oppose the sense granted by this charm increases the target number to oppose the Sidereal by +1 TN.</li> <li>The Sidereal may \u201cfeel\u201d other characters out to medium range around them.</li> <li>Anyone attempting to hide from the Sidereal adds +1 TN to any Stealth or Larceny roll.</li> <li>The Sidereal may see dematerialized spirits.</li> <li>The Sidereal may sense Enemies of Fate with no penalties. So attuned is the Sidereal\u2019s senses to the loom that even the silhouette they normally cast is akin to a highly detailed drawing.</li> <li>The Sidereal is aware of the total health levels the target has.</li> </ul>If the Sidereal uses Heavenly Sentinel Eye while this charm is active, the Sidereal may ask the following questions:<ul><li>What is the weak point of a target?</li> <li>What is the remaining lifespan of a target? (Natural years)</li> <li>Is the target suffering from some sort of illness, poison, non-obvious crippling effect, or other such conditions.</li> <li>How do I kill the target?</li> </ul>This charm heavily strains the Sidereal\u2019s eyes. Upon activating this charm the Sidereal becomes blind for (8 - Essence) hours after activation. Activating this charm again during the cooldown period increases the time from hours to day, while a third time cripples the Sidereal\u2019s eyes rendering them blind until they receive medical attention that requires magical tools. Sidereals who are already blind (or activating this charm when under the discount conditions for Sensing the Strings) are required to pay 6m 1WP to activate this charm for one scene. Since they are used to seeing the world through the Loom of Fate, they do not suffer the blindness of this charm, but activating this charm more than (Essence/2, round up) times per turn risks ruining the adaption for being blind. If the Sidereal exceeds this limit, they\u2019ll need to retrain themselves to be blind for a week again to regain its benefits.<br /> <br /> <b>If Sensing the Strings is seeing Matrix code, then this one allows you to see the world as Neo.<br /> <br /> This is the super sense Sidereal charm, allowing them to sense opponents even who are extremely well hidden. Seeing through solid objects out to medium range is likewise an extremely impressive ability.<br /> <br /> I wanted to keep this up to parity with my Awareness revamp, which means Sidereals get access to Magical senses at Essence 3.<br /> <br /> The issue is that this charm cannot be used repeatedly without consequence. Targets who use sight go blind and are forced to rely on Sensing the Strings. Those who are already blind have more forgiving conditions, but repeated use carries only a small bat instead.\u200b</b><br /> \u200b<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":1183,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","user":"Sandact6","date":". 02-28-2023, 10:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}